Hello All,

I'm fitting a fixed hurdle model (binomial and zeroinflatedpoisson0 ). It's estimated coefficients are virtually identical to PSCL's fixed hurdle (yay!), so the model is being fit correctly as far as I can tell. However, I've spent a good part of the last two days trying to figure out why their predictions are different, and a bit embarrassed that I could not figure it out. I feel one of the following should work, but I don't get results similar to PSCL even with some generous rounding.

pi*lambda   :
pi*(lambda/(1-exp(-lambda)))

I am assuming pi and lambda are the means of from summary.fitted.values. I know technically I should be sampling from the posterior and what I'm doing is only an approximation.

Any help would be so appreciated!

Regards,

Mark

