In-Reply-To: <zcs-ADLYA0k.3EcXGiQzAgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <zcs-ADLYA0k.3EcXGiQzAgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/zcs-ADLYA0k/m/0WUM_GGiAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If you by sqrt you mean

Q=AA

With symmetric A, Like using the sqrt of the eigenvalue and the eigenvector matrix, then no.

If you by sqrt mean

Q=AA’

Then yes, if A is lower-triangular, then this is just the Cholesky factorisation.

H

--
